From 3d3d2a404d6006c1cc75dce7066896e48b3c1999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:52:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 044/104] rule-set: collect garbage after a load only, log
 repeated failures sparingly

A remote rule-set that never came at the start is retried every 30 s (see
"start empty when the first download fails, retry"). Every attempt logged an
error, 2880 a day per list that stays unreachable. Each update tick also
forced a garbage collection, a full pause of the process on a router's CPU,
though a failed or not-modified update leaves nothing to collect.

A rule-set now collects only after an update that loaded a list (and once
when its update loop starts, as before). A series of failed updates logs its
first failure as an error, then once every 10 minutes the count with the
last error, the others at debug; the success after them says how many there
were.
---
